  "problem": {
    "statement": "## Enhancement\nIn containerized deployment environments such as Kubernetes (K8s), container IP addresses change frequently. The current Slow Query Log only records IP information, which is no longer sufficient to track the actual source servers of SQL statements.\n\nTo resolve this issue, we need to record the SESSION_CONNECT_ATTRS information\u2014passed by the client during the handshake phase\u2014into the Slow Query Log. This will allow us to accurately pinpoint the business origin using app_name or other custom tags.",
    "source": "issue",
    "source_url": "https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/issues/66616",
    "source_id": 66616
  },
